# ChkTeX configuration to suppress false-positive warnings
# about the @{} syntax in LaTeX tables

# @{} is standard, valid syntax of the LaTeX kernel
# Warnings about it are false positives and must be suppressed
# See: docs/architecture.md (scripts/ notes) for the background

# Suppress warnings about @{} in column definitions
# These are typically User Regex warnings (numbers 2-8)
# If specific warnings appear, add their numbers here

# Example of a typical configuration:
#   QuietCounter = { 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 }

# Note: if you need to identify the exact number of the warning,
# run: chktex -v1 main.tex
# and look for the warning number related to @{}
